  "title": "More Than 19 Million Eggs Recalled Across Six States After Salmonella Risk Identified",
  "summary": "The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has announced a major egg recall involving more than 19 million eggs distributed across six states due to a potential Salmonella Enteritidis contamination risk. The voluntary recall affects a wide range of egg sizes and popular retail brands sold in grocery stores throughout the southern United States. Consumers who recently purchased eggs in Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Oklahoma, New Mexico, or Arkansas are encouraged to check product information c",
